From d7f520bf8eca94ce3464bc0b70a0619261c04b68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:20:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Compose host-services transport and challengeReplica
 wiring onto the normal Windows tree

Restores the host-services (G1/G2 transport, G3 interface) and G4
challengeReplica wiring that the normal composition omitted, taken from
the installed lease-readiness baseline 32fecf5 only where the file was
absent or the baseline is a strict superset of this tree. Newer normal
sources (lease-gas bundle, host/chain keeper, public-directory,
route-record, lease-reader, relay, supervisor) are kept unchanged.

Generated artifacts (host-service packages, network-runtime bundle,
enclave-wg.exe) are not included.
